+# Todo due dates implementation plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional calendar due dates, UTC overdue status, and overdue-only API/UI filtering for ticket #1.
+
+**Architecture:** Store validated nullable `dueDate` values and derive `overdue` at read time. The API selects overdue items with `?overdue=true`; the existing page renders date/status and reloads the list when its checkbox changes.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24 builtins, node:test, plain HTML/JavaScript, Playwright MCP.
+
+**Spec:** Ticket #1 Approved Spec comment (2026-10-15), agreed in conversation; no separate design file for this small change.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No dependencies; in-memory storage.
+- Invalid dates throw `ValidationError` and yield HTTP 400.
+- `dueDate`: real `YYYY-MM-DD` calendar day or null; POST sets, PATCH changes/removes; omission on PATCH preserves.
+- `overdue`: not done, date present, date strictly before today's UTC date; derived on every API response.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` selects only overdue items; unfiltered/false returns all.
+- Show the word “überfällig” and a “nur überfällige” checkbox; use data-testid for new UI elements.
+- No editing forms or sorting; agent performs end-to-end browser checks and stops the app afterward.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Invalid leap days and timestamps must be rejected, not normalized.
+- Failed PATCH must not partially mutate title, done, or due date.
+- UTC midnight must update status without writing the todo again.
+- Completed, undated, today, and future todos must be excluded by the filter.
+- Fast checkbox changes must not leave stale filtered results on screen.
+
+### Task 1: API due dates and overdue filtering
+
+**Files:** `src/store.mjs`, `src/app.mjs`, `test/store.test.mjs`, `test/app.test.mjs`.
+
+**Interfaces:** `createStore()` retains list/get/add/update/remove; todo responses add `dueDate: string|null` and `overdue: boolean`. `createApp(store)` uses `store.list()` and filters the derived overdue value.
+
+- [x] Write failing store/API tests: date set/change/remove/preserve; invalid date formats/types/calendar days; UTC midnight and done state; atomic invalid updates; mixed-list filtering and empty result. Use fixed dates with node:test mocked Date for boundary tests.
+- [x] Run `npm test`; expect assertion failures for missing date/status/filter behavior.
+- [x] Implement strict date validation and computed snapshots; validate patches before assignment; add query filtering.
+- [x] Run `npm test`; expect all tests passing.
+- [x] Commit API implementation and tests.
+
+### Task 2: List display and overdue checkbox
+
+**Files:** `public/index.html`; browser evidence outside the repo.
+
+**Interfaces:** API from Task 1. New UI test IDs: `overdue-filter`, `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`, `todo-error`.
+
+- [x] Start app on port 3000; wait for `/health`. Seed yesterday/today/future/undated/completed todos via API. With Playwright, assert due-date rendering and filter checkbox; expect failure before implementation.
+- [x] Render dates with semantic time elements, overdue text, and a labelled checkbox. Fetch `/todos?overdue=true` on filter activation; protect against stale responses and show errors accessibly.
+- [x] Run Playwright checks for all date/status cases, filter on/off, changing/removing a date after reload, and fast toggles; save screenshots outside repo. Stop app.
+- [x] Run `npm test` and `git diff --check`; expect success.
+- [x] Commit UI implementation; mark plan complete.
+
+### Close-out
+
+- [x] Obtain independent whole-branch code review; fix important issues with regression tests.
+- [x] Fresh full test run, push branch, open draft PR against main.
+- [x] Post Implementation Summary and Cost Summary to ticket; move to review, leave open.
+
+Completed: independent review found no issues; draft PR http://gitea:3000/adw/demo-todo/pulls/2; implementation/cost summaries posted and ticket #1 moved to review.
